<title>USA: Woolworth says Nike rumor untrue.</title>
<headline>Woolworth says Nike rumor untrue.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Woolworth Corp said a market rumor that its sporting good retail unit, Foot Locker, has reduced it orders from Nike Inc are untrue.</p>
<p>&quot;The rumor is not true. We had a terrific year last year and plans with Nike continue to go forward uninterrupted,&quot; a Woolworth spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>She declined to comment further on the the subject.</p>
<p>Foot Locker is wholly-owned by Woolworth.</p>
<p>Nike shares finished New York Stock Exchange trade off 1/2 at 66-3/8, rising from a session-low 63, while Woolworth ended with a 7/8 gain to 22-3/8.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street Desk, 212-859-1734)).</p>
